WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.634
-I love watching you
on the Knicks

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.000
and I love seeing you
and I do --

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.167
A lot of New Yorkers out there,
we care about the Knicks.

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:08.000
You care about the Knicks.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.501
I don't think anyone cares more
than your 6-year-old son, Kyden.

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:12.667
-Correct. Yes.

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:16.300
-He really, really is passionate
about the Knicks,

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.367
if they win or lose.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:18.400
-Very passionate.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.267
He's -- Everybody thinks,
you know,

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:22.567
playing in New York is hard.

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:24.000
And, you know,
you lose a couple games,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.167
and the media beats on you

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:26.834
and all that different
type of stuff.

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:29.601
Try a car ride home
with my son after a game.

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:31.467
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.567
He -- I mean, it was --
I think it was last year.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:36.934
We had -- I think we maybe won
like 8 or 9 games in a row.

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:37.968
And --
-Let me show who --

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:39.033
-Yes. That's my baby.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.200
-This is the guy
you were talking about.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.334
That's my baby.

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:42.334
-Alright, so,
you're driving home, yeah?

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:46.801
-Yes. Yeah.
Yeah. Driving home.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:49.434
And, you know, we had lost the
game after 8 or 9 in a row,

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:50.968
and he was super-upset
because I guess

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.267
he wanted a 20-game win streak.

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:53.601
I don't know.

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:57.501
And he told me I should ask
for a trade after that.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:59.634
-He's like, "I don't know, dad.
I don't know, dad.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:00.701
I don't think they're
supporting you, dad."

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:01.868
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.901
So, yeah, try try a car ride
home with my son.

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:05.033
It's tough.

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:06.734
-I want to give everyone
an idea of how much

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:08.200
your son cares
about the Knicks.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.968
This is Kyden Randle after the
Knicks lost a preseason game,

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.067
by the way.

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:13.467
This is preseason.
-Not the real thing.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:14.567
-No. Take a look at this.

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:16.534
-[ Crying ]
I don't want to lose.

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:23.334
-Ky, it's just preseason.
-I don't care is it's preseason!

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:26.267
-There's still a chance.
-No, there's not!

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.434
-What?

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:33.801
-Oh, man.

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:36.667
-He's so cute.
He's a cute kid, man.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:37.834
He's a good kid.
-Yeah, he's the best.

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:38.934
He's the best.

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:41.167
-I have a picture of you
as a kid here,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.133
wearing a Kobe jersey
right there.

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:45.300
-Absolutely.
-And...

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.767
[ Applause ]

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:51.467
Kind of cool you got
to play with Kobe.

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.067
-I did. I got to play with Kobe.

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:56.334
As you can see in that picture,
that was my idol growing up.

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:58.834
-And this is you and Kobe.
This is your rookie year.

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:02.868
Look at this. How -- Come on.

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:04.667
-Absolutely.

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:06.701
I mean, come on. This kid --

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:10.167
-Unreal. Unreal.
Who would have thought?

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:11.767
-What was he like?

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:13.100
What was Kobe --
Have you got any Kobe stories?

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.367
What was he...

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.734
-So, this was my first game
back -- in the NBA,

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:20.234
back in my hometown of Dallas.

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:23.801
And, you know, I get there
and I'm excited to go home.

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:26.234
My mom's there. She's cooked.
-Yeah.

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:28.601
You got to see your friends.
-Get to see my friends.

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:30.601
-"Look -- I made it, guys."
-Yeah, party.

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:32.968
You guys are coming to watch me
play tomorrow here, right?

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:34.534
So, I get there,
and Kobe's like,

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:35.667
"No, no, no, no, no.

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:37.534
We're going to the gym

00:02:37.534 --> 00:02:39.501
and we're going to
get a workout in.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:43.000
And, yeah, you can kiss
and wave your hi, you know,

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.400
to your family later,
but, you know, right now,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.868
we're going to get the work in."

00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:51.901
And, unfortunately, after his
passing, I went to the gym --

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:54.601
Shortly after that,
I went to a gym in Detroit.

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:58.167
And the guy who opened up the
gym for me the night before --

00:02:58.167 --> 00:02:59.901
he was like,
"Man, nobody ever does this."

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:02.300
He was like, "The last person
who did this was Kobe."

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.033
-Is that right?
-And -- You know what I mean?

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:07.701
So his spirit is strong.
It's alive and well.

00:03:07.701 --> 00:03:09.267
-Thanks for telling that.
I appreciate that.

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:11.067
[ Applause ]

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:16.367
I got to say, you're amazing
to watch on the court.

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:18.000
You're intimidating to watch.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.167
And I go to the --
I go to the games --

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:21.334
-Me intimidating?
-Yeah.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.801
Yeah, and I look.

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:25.934
I don't want to make eye contact
with you when I go to the game,

00:03:25.934 --> 00:03:27.400
because I don't want to
throw you off or have you,

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.968
like, "Dude,
get Jimmy Fallon out of here,

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:30.033
because that's why
I'm not doing well."

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:31.601
-No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:32.734
-Like, I don't want to say,
"Hi, how are you?",

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:34.033
or do anything.

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:36.033
I just want you to just play.
-We're best friends.

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:38.934
Let's come up with a handshake.
You're good. We're good.

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:40.501
-Yeah. We'll come up
with a cool handshake?

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:41.834
-Let's do it.

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:43.968
-So if I go to the game,
I can just go, "Hey, what's up?

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:45.601
-We got,
"Hey, what's up?", and...

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.367
Let me get a...
-Yeah.

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:50.601
[ Laughter ]
Something like that?

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:51.934
-That's the handshake.
-That's the handshake?

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:54.167
-That's the handshake.
Just once.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.601
-Just once. Just once.
-Just once. Just once.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:58.934
-That's it. That's it.
That's the handshake. We got it.

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:01.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:04.467
It is...
Hey, it's a new season.

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:06.033
You have a new
sneaker partnership.

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:07.801
Tell us about
what you're doing with Skechers.

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:09.701
-You go to work, you want to
work with really good people,

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:11.534
and, you know,
that's the biggest thing.

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:14.200
It's an amazing shoe.
I was really surprised.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.334
You know, I put the shoe on.

00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:17.400
I was working out
in the shoe in the summer,

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.934
and I was like, "Man, this is

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:21.200
the most comfortable shoe
I've ever worn."

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.601
So I'm excited.
They're doing great stuff.

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.567
They're innovative.
They're creative.

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:31.300
-This is you destroying someone.
I'm sorry that...

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.300
Dunking over this --
There's the shoe.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.901
But --
-What's going on?

00:04:35.901 --> 00:04:37.434
-What's going on
in this guy's head?

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:39.133
That's me
when I was at the game.

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:41.901
Yeah, I meant to give you --
What happens after you

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:43.033
do something like this?

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:45.000
You have to apologize to him?

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.200
-No. "This is part of the
business, man." I don't know.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.868
-Wow! That's right!
You go, "Yeah, go to the gym."

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:52.801
-Yeah.
-Go to the gym, dude.

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:55.601
-Nothing personal.
Nothing personal.

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:57.567
I actually got you something.

00:04:57.567 --> 00:05:00.601
You know, I'm saying, you know,
this is new,

00:05:00.601 --> 00:05:02.100
and you like that picture.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:05.634
If you wear these right here --
Okay?

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:08.534
Like those? There you go.
-This is what I'm talking about.

00:05:08.534 --> 00:05:11.133
-Yes. If you wear those, you
will be able to do just that.

00:05:11.133 --> 00:05:12.834
-I can do just that.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:05:12.834 --> 00:05:14.667
-I promise you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:17.434
-Guys, Julius Randle, everybody.

00:05:17.434 --> 00:05:20.400
The Knicks kick off their season
this Wednesday

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:21.968
against the Boston Celtics.

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:23.801
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

